==English==
{{was wotd|2006|June|22}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|post-haste}}, {{l|en|post haste}}
* {{alt|en|postehaste|poste-haste||archaic}}

===Etymology===
From the former instruction on letters ‘haste, post, haste’, later reinterpreted as a compound of {{compound|en|post|haste}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌpəʊstˈheɪst/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌpoʊstˈheɪst/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-posthaste.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-posthaste.ogg|a=AU}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[quickly|Quickly]], as fast as someone travelling post; with great [[speed]].
#: {{ux|en|It is imperative that you finish your task '''posthaste'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1946|author=w:Paramahansa Yogananda|title=s:Autobiography of a Yogi|chapter=Chapter 17|text="Sasi cannot last through the night." These words from his physician, and the spectacle of my friend, now reduced almost to a skeleton, sent me '''posthaste''' to Serampore.}}

